flowchart TB
  accTitle: Bridge private management deployment
  accDescr: Source-defined architecture, not discovered installation. Owner clients access bridged on the Arch host outside K3s. A root helper controls reviewed cluster operations; a separate unprivileged worker builds offline artifacts. Compute traffic does not pass through Bridge.

  owner["Owner browser / bridgectl<br/>Private LAN or owner-managed VPN"]

  subgraph host["SOURCE VIEW · ARCH WORKSTATION — Bridge runs outside K3s"]
    direction TB
    api["bridged · unprivileged<br/>HTTPS API + embedded web UI<br/>Plans, operations and sessions"]
    store[("Bridge persistence<br/>Bounded JSON state + managed source<br/>/var/lib/bridge")]
    helper["bridge-hostd · root<br/>Allowlisted executor<br/>Independent recovery journal"]
    worker["bridge-worker · separate UID<br/>Named offline recipes<br/>Filesystem + cgroup limits"]
    runtime["Installed workstationctl runtime<br/>Shared session lock<br/>GPU release / restore checks"]
    cluster["K3s · single-node workload plane<br/>Restricted helper identity<br/>No automatic qualification"]
    outputs[("Build artifacts + persistent caches<br/>Native llama.cpp HIP / Vulkan<br/>No automatic deployment")]

    api -->|"durable intent / source"| store
    api -->|"Unix socket · peer UID checked"| helper
    api -->|"Unix socket · peer UID checked"| worker
    helper -->|"fixed operations / verified files"| runtime
    helper -->|"TLS API · scoped RBAC"| cluster
    worker -->|"bounded builds"| outputs
  end

  owner -->|"Dedicated HTTPS hostname · authenticated"| api

  classDef authority fill:#fff0eb,stroke:#ad5439,color:#47251a
